This patch is needed because Solaris C++ headers and compiler behavior expose a
char versus int8_t specialization clash in the generated Temporal C API helper
header.

What it does:
- skips the conflicting String converter specialization on Solaris

Why it is needed:
- without it, the C++ binding header fails to compile due to duplicate
  specialization logic

--- a/v8-146.4.0/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/temporal_capi-v0_1/bindings/cpp/temporal_rs/diplomat_runtime.hpp
+++ b/v8-146.4.0/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/temporal_capi-v0_1/bindings/cpp/temporal_rs/diplomat_runtime.hpp
@@ -389,5 +389,7 @@
 MAKE_SLICE_CONVERTERS(F64, double)
 MAKE_SLICE_CONVERTERS(Bool, bool)
 MAKE_SLICE_CONVERTERS(Char, char32_t)
+#if !defined(__sun)
 MAKE_SLICE_CONVERTERS(String, char)
+#endif
 MAKE_SLICE_CONVERTERS(String16, char16_t)
